{
 "slug": "pick-where-to-hide-from-a-tornado",
 "title": "Pick where to hide from a tornado: under an overpass, in your car, in a mobile home, or in the basement",
 "format": "pick-a-scenario",
 "root": "/home/claude/b3d/tornado",
 "lines": [
  "Only one of these is the safe spot.",
  "Pick one: a tornado is coming. Where do you hide?",
  "Under an overpass, in your car, in a mobile home, or in the basement.",
  "Pick one, two, three or four, and comment. Quick.",
  "Number one, under a highway overpass. It feels like a concrete bunker.",
  "But the narrow gap can speed the [wind](winnd) up, and fill it with flying debris.",
  "In Oklahoma in [1999](nineteen ninety-nine), people died sheltering under overpasses.",
  "Number two, your car. Just drive away, right?",
  "Experts say never try to outrun a tornado. Cars get tossed and crushed.",
  "If it's on top of you, get out and lie flat in a ditch, covering your head.",
  "Number three, a mobile home. Most tornadoes can destroy one, even tied down.",
  "You're fifteen to twenty times more likely to die in one than in a regular house.",
  "Number four, the basement. This is the winner.",
  "Get underground, under something sturdy, away from windows.",
  "No basement? A small inside room on the lowest floor, like a bathroom or closet.",
  "Put as many walls as you can between you and the outside.",
  "Cover your head. Flying debris is the greatest danger.",
  "In that same storm, radar clocked about three hundred miles per hour.",
  "That's almost double the [wind](wind) of a [Category 5](Category five) hurricane.",
  "That's almost double the [wind](winnd) of a [Category 5](Category five) hurricane."
 ],
